{"toolCallId":"call_e1acddf10f5e443aac804ecd7e10a4c8","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"9:_placeholder_rule_dir=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"${BASH_SOURCE[0]}\")\" && pwd)\"\n11:source \"${_placeholder_rule_dir}/../lib/status-classifier.sh\"\n15:# Description: Detects unfilled spec-doc placeholders: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE:], [NEEDS_CLARIFICATION:] / [NEEDS CLARIFICATION:],\n17:#   are soft by design, and neither this rule nor spec/check-placeholders.sh flags them.\n19:#   [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: ...] token. While spec.md has the Status Draft, an unfilled token in such a doc is a\n21:#   always had. [NEEDS_CLARIFICATION:] is an error in every packet.\n24:# indented fence, the <YOUR_VALUE_HERE: form and a [template: title; production runs\n25:# only the orchestrator. Mustache {{...}} is NOT flagged (not canonical spec-doc placeholder\n27:# spec/check-placeholders.sh, the post-edit scan, reads its markers through\n28:# placeholder_marker_lines below so it reports what strict validation flags.\n34:# Prints one \"line<TAB>kind\" row for each line holding an unfilled marker, read\n36:# on the line is a [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: value token, \"marker\" when any other marker\n42:placeholder_marker_lines() {\n71:        BEGIN { in_code = 0; marker = \"<YOUR_VALUE_HERE:|\\\\[YOUR_VALUE_HERE:|\\\\[NEEDS[_ ]CLARIFICATION:\" }\n84:                    if (substr(rest, RSTART, RLENGTH) != \"[YOUR_VALUE_HERE:\") hard = 1\n124:    local -a found_placeholders=()\n171:                    found_placeholders+=(\"$file:$linenum\")\n173:            done < <(placeholder_marker_lines \"$filepath\" v23)\n185:        # Pattern 1: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE:] (skip inline backticks)\n195:                    found_placeholders+=(\"$file:$linenum\")\n198:        done < <(echo \"$filtered\" | grep -E '\\[YOUR_VALUE_HERE:' 2>/dev/null | \\\n199:                 grep -v '`\\[YOUR_VALUE_HERE:' | \\\n200:                 grep -v '\\[YOUR_VALUE_HERE:[^]]*\\]`' || true)\n202:        # Pattern 2: [NEEDS_CLARIFICATION:] / [NEEDS CLARIFICATION:] (underscore + space)\n207:                found_placeholders+=(\"$file:$linenum\")\n220:                found_placeholders+=(\"$file:$linenum\")\n226:    local -a unique_placeholders=()\n228:    if [[ ${#found_placeholders[@]} -gt 0 ]]; then\n229:        for item in \"${found_placeholders[@]}\"; do\n232:                unique_placeholders+=(\"$item\")\n=== my spec placeholders\n103:| REQ-001 | `--quiet` writes exactly one line to stdout, `Recommended Level: <N> (<Name>)`, and exits 0. |\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w8f3d32b7e3/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"0cc9a2","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
